# Runs before every commit. Any failing step stops the commit. These are the
# floors CLAUDE.md asks to defend: lint at zero, every test passing, and
# package.json and package-lock.json agreeing. `git commit --no-verify` skips
# all of it — use it only when you mean to.
#
# Typecheck and tests run on the whole working tree, not only the staged
# files, so an unstaged edit can still fail them. That costs a second; it's
# cheaper than a commit that passes here and breaks on a clean checkout.

node scripts/check-lockfile.mjs
npx lint-staged
npx tsc --noEmit
npm test
